## 🔬 Mathematical Architecture

The **HPWM (High-Precision Wave Mechanics)** model couples three nonlinear field sectors:
1. **Chiral Orientation Sector ($S^3 \simeq \mathrm{SU}(2)$):** Unit 4-vector $n^A(x) \in \mathbb{R}^4$ with $n^A n^A = 1$ in the hedgehog ansatz $n^A = (\sin F(r)\hat{r}^i, \cos F(r))$.
2. **Dilatonic Scalar $\chi(x) \in \mathbb{R}$:** Modulating the effective pion decay constant $f^2(\chi) = f_0^2 + \zeta \chi^2$.
3. **Higgs Scalar $h(x) \in \mathbb{R}$:** Driving spontaneous gauge symmetry breaking.

### Mozga-Dirac 5-Field Fluctuation Operator
Around the static topological soliton ($B=1$), fluctuations decompose into **5 radial channels** across grand-spin sectors $K = \vec{I} + \vec{J}$:
$$q(r, t) = \big( a(r, t), \, b(r, t), \, c(r, t), \, x(r, t), \, y(r, t) \big)^T,$$
governed by the tensor wave equation:
$$-\mathcal{K}_{\text{loc}}(r) \frac{\partial^2 q}{\partial t^2} + \frac{\partial}{\partial r}\left( \mathcal{K}_{\text{der}}(r) \frac{\partial q}{\partial r} \right) - \mathcal{C}(r) q = 0.$$

